{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DUz4WU5nFCFynnZ2JEzaY3","type":"tool_result","content":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*_test.go\n5:## Summary\n22:## Architecture\n25:flowchart TD\n44:## Stack\n48:## Label state machine\n95:## The .ard/ contract\n175:## Open issues\n189:## Scanners\n263:## Triage loop\n304:## Executors and the Reaper\n352:## Worker loop\n372:## Reviewer loop\n407:## Merger loop\n432:## PR watch loop\n446:## Configuration\n520:## Guardrails\n547:## Gaps in the original sketch\n567:## Delivery\n580:## Rollout\n585:flowchart LR\n609:## Open questions\n136:**Network round re-run (#3\n**Network round re-run (#386).** A round is open while the newest bounced worker has no triage engineer `done` after it (job ID order). `Prepare` persists the round in the job record (`NetworkState.Round`, `Done`, `Rerun`), so `Build` stays pure and Resume replays the same plan. The engineer's first `done` in a round consumes it: its close-out clears `ard:triage:lead:done` (`Plan.Clear`, removed in the request phase before the requests are added, 404 counting as success) and adds `ard:pending`, so the lead runs first, and persists the other triage roles that had finished `done` (`Plan.Rerun`). The lead's close-out in that round re-requests those roles and clears their `:done` (roles no longer configured are skipped), so all finish before the gate. A human re-request of the engineer sees no open round and does not re-arm again. The engineer may declare `inputs:` (`path`, `provider` `human` or `worker`, optional https `url`), parsed from the redacted role file and stored in the plan. The gate checks each path (plain characters, clean and relative, not under `.ard/`, `.github/` or `.git`), reads main once per tick at one SHA through `ls-tree` (no content, regular blobs only, size capped, cached per SHA) and holds with a \"waiting for inputs\" comment listing each missing path and the capture-note format until every human-provided input exists. A `worker` input with a `network: false` worker role, a bad path or an oversized file ends `needs-human`. A network round always requires a fresh approval, even with `require_approval: false` and even when the engineer removed every network need: the \"ready for approval\" marker gains a `round=<n>`, and an earlier approval is stale because the engineer's new `:done` follows it. An approval given while inputs are missing still counts once they land. Label state machine: the engineer's `done` close-out removes `ard:triage:lead:done` and adds `ard:pending` before its own `:done`; the lead's close-out removes `:done` from each re-opened role and requests it again; the gate does not run while the lead's `:done` is absent. The gate records one `wait` gate event when it starts waiting for inputs and one `inputs-ready` event when they land; the daily status-issue digest shows a *Waiting for inputs* count of open issues whose newest gate event is the wait.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"015b7330-5d47-4bab-a218-7f9c713b26a1","uuid":"00090797-130d-48b4-bf15-b88b8e07dbf9","timestamp":"2026-11-25T15:31:07.453Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*_test.go\n5:## Summary\n22:## Architecture\n25:flowchart TD\n44:## Stack\n48:## Label state machine\n95:## The .ard/ contract\n175:## Open issues\n189:## Scanners\n263:## Triage loop\n304:## Executors and the Reaper\n352:## Worker loop\n372:## Reviewer loop\n407:## Merger loop\n432:## PR watch loop\n446:## Configuration\n520:## Guardrails\n547:## Gaps in the original sketch\n567:## Delivery\n580:## Rollout\n585:flowchart LR\n609:## Open questions\n136:**Network round re-run (#3\n**Network round re-run (#386).** A round is open while the newest bounced worker has no triage engineer `done` after it (job ID order). `Prepare` persists the round in the job record (`NetworkState.Round`, `Done`, `Rerun`), so `Build` stays pure and Resume replays the same plan. The engineer's first `done` in a round consumes it: its close-out clears `ard:triage:lead:done` (`Plan.Clear`, removed in the request phase before the requests are added, 404 counting as success) and adds `ard:pending`, so the lead runs first, and persists the other triage roles that had finished `done` (`Plan.Rerun`). The lead's close-out in that round re-requests those roles and clears their `:done` (roles no longer configured are skipped), so all finish before the gate. A human re-request of the engineer sees no open round and does not re-arm again. The engineer may declare `inputs:` (`path`, `provider` `human` or `worker`, optional https `url`), parsed from the redacted role file and stored in the plan. The gate checks each path (plain characters, clean and relative, not under `.ard/`, `.github/` or `.git`), reads main once per tick at one SHA through `ls-tree` (no content, regular blobs only, size capped, cached per SHA) and holds with a \"waiting for inputs\" comment listing each missing path and the capture-note format until every human-provided input exists. A `worker` input with a `network: false` worker role, a bad path or an oversized file ends `needs-human`. A network round always requires a fresh approval, even with `require_approval: false` and even when the engineer removed every network need: the \"ready for approval\" marker gains a `round=<n>`, and an earlier approval is stale because the engineer's new `:done` follows it. An approval given while inputs are missing still counts once they land. Label state machine: the engineer's `done` close-out removes `ard:triage:lead:done` and adds `ard:pending` before its own `:done`; the lead's close-out removes `:done` from each re-opened role and requests it again; the gate does not run while the lead's `:done` is absent. The gate records one `wait` gate event when it starts waiting for inputs and one `inputs-ready` event when they land; the daily status-issue digest shows a *Waiting for inputs* count of open issues whose newest gate event is the wait.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DUz4WU5nFCFynnZ2JEzaY3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
